---
description: SQL models in db/models
globs: db/models/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Start every model with a comment stating its grain, e.g. "one row per quote_id".
- Event tables (like analytics.payoff_events) have one row per event. Aggregate to the grain before joining.
- Dates: convert timestamptz with AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Jakarta' before taking the date. Never bucket in UTC.
- No PII columns: no NIK, phone, email, name or bank account. borrower_id only.
- Every model ships with checks as SQL queries that return zero rows: uniqueness of the grain, not-null on required columns.
